# Lick: Vibrato (repertoire plan: st-lick-vibrato). An original 8-bar slow blues in A minor
# (Am7 Am7 | Dm7 Dm7 | Am7 E7 | Am7 Am7), in A minor pentatonic box 1. Short runs lead to long
# notes held for two beats with vibrato: A on string 1 fret 5 (finger 1), G on string 2 fret 8
# (finger 3) and D on string 3 fret 7 (finger 3), each heard at more than one speed:
#   bars 1-2: 2 waves per beat (eighth notes: A, then G),
#   bars 3-4: 3 waves per beat (triplets: D, then A),
#   bars 5-8: 4 waves per beat (sixteenths: G, D, A, and the last A on string 4).
# A wave is one push away from the note and back. Keep it in time with the beat, and let the pitch
# rise only a little: on strings 2 and 3 push the string up, on string 1 pull it down.
# The quick G notes in the runs use finger 4; the long Gs use finger 3, the strongest finger.
title: Lick: Vibrato
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original lick in A minor pentatonic, box 1
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: vibrato, slow blues, minor pentatonic, box 1, lick
